21	// inlining is that these SVGs pick that font up for free once embedded in a page that serves it,
22	// with no embedding/subsetting/data-URI of their own.
23	//
24	// The four metrics are read from VictorMonoNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf (the Mono patched variant
25	// static/fonts/VictorMono.ttf ships - see the note above the @font-face in src/css/custom.css for
26	// why that variant): the svg package's --cell-width/--line-height defaults are Hack Nerd Font's
27	// ratios (src/svg/svg.go's defaultCellWidth/defaultLineHeight), correct for the CLI's own default
28	// font stack but wrong for Victor Mono, which this build actually renders in. Passing these
29	// explicitly keeps the grid math (column advance, row height) matched to the font the browser will
30	// actually lay the text out in.
31	//
32	// CELL_WIDTH: ASCII 'M' advance 600 / unitsPerEm 1100 = 0.5455em.
33	// LINE_HEIGHT: hhea (Ascender - Descender + LineGap) 1550 / unitsPerEm 1100 =
34	// 1.4091em, times 1.2 (the retired PNG renderer's own lineSpacing constant,
